{"id": "EUVD-2026-59502", "enisaUuid": "cc6fc4a2-6d06-3e34-91e4-ed11ec0089be", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/vt-d: Fix RB-tree corruption in probe error path\n\nThe info->node RB-tree member is zero-initialized via kzalloc. If\na device does not support ATS, the device_rbtree_insert() call is\nskipped. If a subsequent probe step fails, the error path jumps to\ndevice_rbtree_remove(), which misinterprets the zeroed node as\na tree root and corrupts the device RB-tree.\n\nFix this by explicitly initializing the RB-node as empty using\nRB_CLEAR_NODE() during initialization and guarding the removal with\nRB_EMPTY_NODE().", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:35", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5102e0fc3c6dc8685549891a96e4589fdb3e211", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d16923a45d4d08367650fdc3451c89299ab6ac5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43bd9e6d5513cb1edbafdeef146a1edc3aaced56"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74355", "GHSA-444c-98p8-5jq5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2f1a609a-5abd-392e-8c27-cd66d69470a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1492efb495bcef34c9ee8a94af81e6cea5abf4 <f5102e0fc3c6dc8685549891a96e4589fdb3e211"}, {"id": "3ef16de3-ceb1-3605-8844-d456c8d1ae4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "44368b38-a1a0-3abd-bb76-2dce14ea76e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "91fe88de-4d00-37c7-a9e5-d71683033efa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "a269293f-38fb-362e-b329-cf6c69706437", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1492efb495bcef